From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: apply a localized msstyles' string table values

Purpose: use the fonts that the Japanese Luna theme defines for Japanese.
XP behavior: a localized msstyles keeps per-language values in its string
table, as "NormalBlue@[Rebar]Font=MS UI Gothic, 9" for the colour and size
variant whose ini resource is NORMALBLUE_INI, and applies them over the ini.
Wine before: read only the ini, so the Japanese XP shell got Tahoma 8 and
Franklin Gothic Medium where XP uses MS UI Gothic, and the Start panel was
laid out 20 pixels narrower.
Change: when the theme is parsed, read the string table entries of the
selected variant, substitute matching ini values (including [SysMetrics])
and add the ones the ini lacks. The values are read from the user's theme
file at run time.
Evidence: all 117 TMT_FONT values of 26 classes reported by
tests/theme-props.c --fonts equal the reference XP machine's.
Scope: only with WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL.
Old patches: 0058.
---
 dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c | 145 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.h |   2 +
 2 files changed, 145 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

